  "question": "Does this exact sole revision resolve all four r1 defects and preserve original operational behavior sufficiently for ONE nominal diagnostic, subject to separate fresh owner handoff and source/resource admission?",
  "requirements": [
    "D154 actual failure must remain; exact cause unknown until observation",
    "D155 approved v3 counter-fit source; its review budget remains consumed",
    "Unique complete candidate FD-row join before correlation; no selector/topology changes",
    "Original predicates/tool outcomes/full archive and restore/terminal cleanup/resource limits preserved",
    "Current source/tool/runtime/original-output pins and storage-owner handoff required before launch"
  ],
  "review_scope": "Read-only immutable packet, source and preserved raw synthetic evidence. Up to60s aggregate bounded pure/in-memory checks per reviewer, no filesystem writes/pycache/receipt-writing mains, no actual IPC/mount/probe/guard/compiler/proof/storage/network operation. Inspect test entrypoints before reusing them.",
  "review_points": [
    "Counter/count/index/hash/FD/join correctness and ambiguity/incompleteness refusals",
    "Bounded parser/archive/summary behavior and malformed input errors",
    "Preserved parent terminal exit and failure precedence; optional result cannot override final stdout",
    "Literal-only guard changes and inherited scope/lock cancellation and limits",
    "Complete-retention evidence is conditional on actual independently read-back receipt chain; no same-UID authenticity or formal proof claim",
    "Retain old archive compatibility and distinguish authenticated fixed producer reachability from malformed consumer counterexamples",
    "Check short single-purpose new functions, finite loops and resource caps; inherited trusted runtime/OS limits remain explicit"
  ],
  "revision_policy": "This is the one allowed evidence-driven revision. No further repair/review reset if mandatory defects remain. D155 v3 independent revision budget stays zero.",
  "prior_current_peer_verdicts": "NONE; both fresh reviewers receive this same packet before any current peer report",
